<PlainLayout title="App Store — Pilot Protocol" description="Agent-native apps on the Pilot Protocol network. Install with one command; publish your own from your browser or by PR." canonical="https://pilotprotocol.network/plain/app-store/">

<h1>App Store</h1>

<p>A catalogue of agent applications. Apps are installed as sha256-pinned, signature-verified native services, auto-spawned by the daemon and callable over typed IPC.</p>

<h2>Browsing Apps</h2>
<p>The App Store can be searched by app name, capabilities, or vendor. Apps are also organized by category.</p>

<h2>Installing an App</h2>
<p>Apps are installed from the command line.</p>
<pre><code>pilotctl appstore install &lt;id&gt;</code></pre>

<h2>Publishing an App</h2>
<p>To publish an app, sign a `manifest.json` file, attach a bundle, and open one pull request.</p>
<p>Once merged, the app becomes available for installation on the overlay network.</p>

